  "scope": "One separate-context AI built a new local Field Notes app from an empty project, using the displayed brief and public references. Another AI reviewed and replayed it. Same host and tools; no prior conversation or existing local implementation provided to the builder. This is not a security sandbox or an external-company adoption study. Completion review added erasure, explicit fixture capability declarations and full local conformance. The current documentation brief has been strengthened since the original prompt recorded below.",
  "prompt": "Integrate OpenIAP Commerce Protocol into this project.\nProduct and desired behavior: Field Notes is a subscription notes app. Build a local browser demo where Alice can buy Premium, cancel renewal while keeping paid access, and lose access at expiry. Bob must not be able to take Alice’s purchase..\nServices to use or own: Own the commerce backend and event receiver. Use fictional purchases and local fixture users for this first review; no external accounts or credentials. Choose a small stack for this empty project..\n\nReference: https://github.com/hyodotdev/openiap-commerce-protocol-example\nRead INTEGRATE.md for my role; follow BUILD.md for a commerce backend.\nInspect this project's instructions and stack. Install openiap-commerce-protocol; use its SPEC.md, generated bindings/schemas, and conformance tools as the contract.\n\nImplement the connection using existing project patterns. Start with a runnable local result. Run the applicable success and failure checks, fix failures, and rerun them.\nShow the running URL and user-visible outcomes, with source and verification commands for future changes. Separate fixture evidence from real store/deployment checks; list remaining work and product decisions.\nKeep changes uncommitted for review.\n",
